type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* The tags shown on a tiddler keep the order you added them in, rather than being sorted alphabetically. Position can carry meaning. Eg: the first tag reads as the most important, and tags placed next to each other read as belonging together
* Lists showing every tag in the wiki, such as the $:/TagManager and the sidebar ''More > Tags'' tab, stay sorted alphabetically and are unaffected
* The order is configurable under ''Control Panel'' > ''Settings'' > ''Tag Sorting'': do not sort, sort alphabetically, or supply your own filter
* While the order is unsorted, a tag in the tiddler editor can be dragged to a new position
* A custom filter can also hide tags. `[!prefix[.]]` on a tiddler's tags hides every tag whose name begins with a dot, which keeps working tags out of a reader facing view
* `[tags[]]` returns tags in the order they appear on the tiddler. Previously a tag that looks like a whole number, such as a year, jumped to the front of the result
* `<$action-listops>` no longer rewrites the whole `tags` field in alphabetical order when it adds or removes a tag
